---
// Our Story: 1637 heritage, free house, and revival narrative.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
import storyImg from '../assets/photos/story-interior.jpg';
---

<section id="story" class="bg-white px-5 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Est. 1637" title="Our Story">
      {/* ship icon */}
      <svg class="h-6 w-6" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 15l1.6 3.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.8 1.1h11.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.8-1.1L21 15M5 15h14l-2-4H7l-2 4zM12 3v8M12 3l3 2M12 3L9 5" />
      </svg>
    </SectionHeader>

    <div data-reveal-group class="mt-12 grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-14">
      <div data-reveal class="mx-auto w-full overflow-hidden rounded-2xl shadow-soft ring-1 ring-navy/10">
        <Image
          src={storyImg}
          alt="A snug corner of The Old Ship: a low beam painted 'Duck or Grouse', a cushioned window seat looking onto the garden, and a worn oak table set for a chat"
          widths={[480, 768, 1100]}
          sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 50vw, 100vw"
          loading="lazy"
          class="max-h-[34rem] w-full object-cover object-top transition duration-500 motion-safe:hover:scale-[1.03]"
        />
      </div>

      <div data-reveal class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
        <p>
          Tucked just off the Marlow Road in the village of Cadmore End, The Old Ship is the sort of
          pub England does best, with low oak beams, open fires and no airs about it. There's been an
          inn on this spot <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">since 1637</strong>, which means beer
          has been poured here for the best part of four centuries.
        </p>
        <p>
          For generations it was the heart of the village, and after a long spell with its doors
          closed, it's open once more, back to doing what it always did well, serving honest food,
          well-kept ale and good company. We've kept the old charm people remember, restoring as much
          of the original building as we could.
        </p>
        <p>
          Being a <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">free house</strong> means we can pour what we
          like, and what we like is mostly on our doorstep, from breweries just down the road.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* The owner's own words on what the pub is for, and a thank-you to everyone
        who helped reopen it. Given a tinted panel so it reads as a statement. */}
    <div
      data-reveal
      class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-2xl rounded-2xl border-t-2 border-gold bg-paper px-6 py-8 text-center sm:px-10"
    >
      <p class="font-serif text-2xl italic leading-relaxed text-navy sm:text-3xl">
        It matters to us that the pub stays a pub: somewhere anyone can come for a drink or two and
        spend time with others.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
        Thank you to everyone who has worked on The Old Ship and supported us along the way to get
        her sailing again in Cadmore End. We look forward to welcoming you soon.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
